{"kind":"propose","text":"E2 proposal for the one declared-scope MCP explore tool. Add one value export at @generalbusiness/dap-client/scope:\n\nexport function explore\u003cD extends DeclaredDefinition, K extends Kind\u003cD\u003e\u003e(\n  replica: Replica\u003cD\u003e, key: string, act: PartialAct\u003cD, K\u003e,\n  authority: { readonly session: Session, readonly requestedAt: Timestamp },\n  clock: () =\u003e Timestamp,\n): Promise\u003cExploration\u003cD, K\u003e\u003e\n\nMCP supplies the existing C2 replica, the checked ES-1 Session and its paired host request-start timestamp, and the host clock. The reader must use the identical session, and the replica rechecks the full scope and membership, actor, member, session expiry, and head/generation after awaits. The result shows the standing, its Membership head, session end, clock and the request-start timestamp. The nonnegative local elapsed time bounds the age of the observation assuming a monotonic host clock. A backwards clock, replaced/expired session or missing standing makes authority unavailable. The result carries no credential and claims no fresh native grant.\n\nThe export returns the private replica exploration result. The client passes the checked value through the existing judgeExploreGrant and shared E1 judgeActBody. It leaves the C4 caller signature and native judgment unchanged. Missing source, unsupported evidence and a moved cut retain the corresponding unavailable case. Add no ScopeApi method, route, derive change or Membership replica. The scope never consumes a presented grant.\n\nThe caller is the declared tool at packages/mcp/src/service.ts. Its closed input is { target: ScopeId, key: string, act: { kind: string, on: number | null, fields: object, expected?: Record\u003cstring, number\u003e } }. Resolve target to the reader's full pinned scope, derive field shape and declared kinds from the existing Section 10 per-act descriptor, and support incomplete fields. The tool bounds and returns result data and, for an admitted result, the complete changed-row delta from after. A delta that exceeds the bound returns unavailable. Caller arguments provide no authority, clock, replica or pending assumptions.\n\nFiles are packages/client/src/scope.ts, replica.ts, replica-explore.ts, act-context.ts, act-types.ts, act-explore.ts, session.ts and reads.ts, plus packages/mcp/src/service.ts and the existing inventory/session reader and owning tests. Reds compare the real declared MCP call and private E1/native results at one cut, context and clock. Hold the cut fixed and change the checked standing and clock independently. Refuse absent, wrong, moved and expired session/cut, malformed tool arguments, unavailable source and oversized results. Record no signature, write, or submission during exploration.\n\nRequest approval of this interface and witness scope. Source follows LV5 and O2.","body":{"to":"planner"}}